  "authors": [],
  "body": {
    "comment": "Summary\nEMURGO as a DRep votes YES on the treasury withdrawal titled \"\"PFMS: Bringing Government Scale Adoption to Cardano by Trivolve Tech\"\", with the rationale outlined below.\n\nRationale\nWhile EMURGO has maintained a cautious, selective approach to discretionary treasury spending during ongoing ecosystem considerations, we recognize this proposal as a high-impact strategic imperative for Cardano's global institutional footprint.\n\nThe deployment of the Police & Forensic Management System (PFMS) represents a tangible milestone for real-world enterprise adoption. Securing state-level criminal justice workflows on Cardano validates our layer-1 architecture as institutional-grade infrastructure while generating over 1.5 million verified mainnet transactions annually. Furthermore, the engagement of the Cardano Foundation as the off-chain administrator provides the necessary accountability, milestone gating, and operational rigor required for capital allocations of this magnitude.\n\nCrucially, the economic model aligns with long-term treasury sustainability by returning 70% of third-party verification revenues back to the Cardano Treasury and allocating 20% to core open-source library maintenance. Supporting this proposal directly advances Cardano's competitive enterprise position and drives measurable utility. For these reasons, EMURGO votes yes."
  },
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256"
}